²/(2 E Phi_xx³), and mu(dt)=gamma′(t)dt. For 0<t<1, 2 gamma′ E Phi_xx³≥gamma(t)² E Phi_xx⁴/1000>0. Only gamma′(0)≥0 is asserted at zero. Since E Phi_xx²=1 and Phi_xx>=0, moment Cauchy–Schwarz gives E Phi_xx³<=sqrt(E Phi_xx⁴)<=E Phi_xx⁴. Hence gamma′(t)>=gamma(t)²/2000 for 0<t<1, and mu((r,s])>=(s-r)gamma(r)²/2000 for 0<r<s<1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"field:44ce9c691552a5cbf2cc1ab59116063095b9cb2bed4c3a9313fb53db9f891c13","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686